---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Person structured data — /about is the canonical identity page for the site.
const person = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Trent Jones',
  url: 'https://rtrentjones.dev/about/',
  jobTitle: 'Senior Software Development Engineer',
  worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Audible' },
  alumniOf: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'University of Southern California' },
  sameAs: ['https://github.com/RTrentJones', 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/rtrentjones'],
};
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Trent Jones, a software engineer in Los Angeles who builds side projects out of curiosity."
  prose
  structuredData={person}
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Trent. I'm a software engineer based in Los Angeles, currently working at Audible on the
    Creator side of the business.
  </p>

  <p>
    Before that I spent most of my time at Amazon working on Alexa, across web, mobile, backend
    services, developer tooling, and the machinery required to actually ship all of it.
  </p>
  <p>
    I started my career at <a href="https://www.fulgentgenetics.com/">Fulgent Genetics</a>, when the
    company was still small enough that being a software engineer meant working on whatever the lab
    needed: the LIMS, tools for variant curation and clinical reporting, and the patient-facing
    portal. I studied neuroscience and computer science at USC, so that part of my background has
    never really disappeared. <a href="/bamcp/">BAMCP</a> is probably the most obvious example of it
    showing back up.
  </p>

  <p>
    Outside work, I tend to build things because I want them to exist or because implementing
    something seems like the best way to understand it.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/pg_kafka/">pg_kafka</a> started with me taking an argument about Postgres a little too
    seriously. <a href="/heistmind/">HeistMind</a> was a tool I wanted for a tabletop game.
    <a href="/greenlight/">Greenlight</a> came later, after I realized I'd rebuilt essentially the
    same deployment and verification setup for several different projects.
  </p>
  <p>
    This site is where I keep those things and occasionally write about what I learned building them.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also find me on <a href="https://github.com/RTrentJones">GitHub</a> and
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rtrentjones">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
